WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:13.973
"I'm burning!"

2
00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:15.174
Zann screamed.

3
00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:19.377
Only his head and shoulders were above the hot, bubbling water.

4
00:00:20.278 --> 00:00:21.719
His friends were screaming too.

5
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.302
But Zann could only think about his own searing pain.

6
00:00:26.303 --> 00:00:28.024
A sharp whistle came from overhead.

7
00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:32.528
Zing was flying back and forth between the kids and the rocky shore.

8
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.821
Being a fire dragon, Zing was immune to heat and had already shaken off the hot water.

9
00:00:39.562 --> 00:00:41.602
Seeing Zing cleared Zann's mind a little.

10
00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:45.343
The wormhole was over their heads—too high to reach.

11
00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:47.584
The shore was pretty far away.

12
00:00:48.504 --> 00:00:51.585
There was only one way he and his friends would survive this.

13
00:00:51.605 --> 00:00:53.766
"Focus, everyone!"

14
00:00:54.006 --> 00:00:54.566
Zann yelled.

15
00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:57.587
"We have to zap out of the water!"

16
00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:01.188
He hoped their magic would work in this world.

17
00:01:01.788 --> 00:01:04.577
If not He tried not to think about it.

18
00:01:05.658 --> 00:01:07.439
"Everyone join hands!"

19
00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:08.420
Gliss cried.

20
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.182
Zann felt someone grab his hand.

21
00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:15.084
He almost yanked it away because the touch hurt his injured skin.

22
00:01:15.785 --> 00:01:17.606
He forced himself to squeeze back though.

23
00:01:17.626 --> 00:01:19.647
"Zap!" he cried.

24
00:01:20.848 --> 00:01:22.689
He landed on the rocky shore with a grunt.

25
00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.591
The heat was gone.

26
00:01:25.071 --> 00:01:26.632
Well, some of it was gone.

27
00:01:27.513 --> 00:01:31.956
Looking around, Zann could see that they were in a world of flame and scorching heat.

28
00:01:32.736 --> 00:01:35.157
A fiery red sky hung overhead.

29
00:01:35.997 --> 00:01:37.677
Steam rose from the bubbling lake.

30
00:01:38.518 --> 00:01:41.599
Zann could already feel sweat beading on his burned skin.

31
00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:45.740
But at least he no longer felt as if his whole body were melting.

32
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.461
Gliss rubbed her hands together, wincing at the pain.

33
00:01:50.101 --> 00:01:51.621
Then she touched Darb.

34
00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:57.403
"Heal!" Instantly Darb's skin went from fiery red to its normal color.

35
00:01:57.423 --> 00:02:01.504
"Thanks," he said, slumping with relief.

36
00:02:02.536 --> 00:02:04.298
Gliss quickly healed herself next.

37
00:02:04.838 --> 00:02:06.039
Zann and Perda did the same.

38
00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.001
"That was close."

39
00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:09.362
Perda looked around.

40
00:02:09.382 --> 00:02:11.384
"What world is this?"

41
00:02:11.404 --> 00:02:14.226
"I don't know," said Zann.

42
00:02:15.147 --> 00:02:17.869
Zing landed, and Zann scratched the dragon's head.

43
00:02:17.889 --> 00:02:20.171
"Thanks for the help, little buddy."

44
00:02:21.212 --> 00:02:23.053
Zing chirped, sounding nervous.

45
00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:25.775
A large shadow passed over the group.

46
00:02:26.656 --> 00:02:30.820
Glancing up, Zann saw an enormous dragon flying overhead.

47
00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:33.889
Luckily it didn't seem to notice them.

48
00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:37.791
"We need to figure out whether Wyssa is here," Perda said.

49
00:02:37.811 --> 00:02:43.854
"Quickly." Zann and his friends picked their way carefully up the rocky slope.

50
00:02:44.674 --> 00:02:45.935
"There goes another dragon."

51
00:02:46.435 --> 00:02:50.817
Darb shaded his eyes to watch a shadowy creature fly by in the distance.

52
00:02:51.577 --> 00:02:52.237
"Look out!"

53
00:02:52.758 --> 00:02:54.679
Gliss grabbed Darb and yanked him back.

54
00:02:54.699 --> 00:02:57.460
"You almost stepped in that puddle!"

55
00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:02.107
Zann wasn't sure why she sounded so anxious until he looked down.

56
00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:06.771
Right near his feet was a puddle of burning hot lava!

57
00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:10.374
"Everyone be careful," Perda warned.

58
00:03:11.355 --> 00:03:12.315
They continued walking.

59
00:03:13.236 --> 00:03:15.398
Several more dragons flew by in the distance.

60
00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:20.302
The only other signs of life were a few scrubby trees and shrubs.

61
00:03:20.322 --> 00:03:24.065
"This is crazy," Perda said after a few minutes.

62
00:03:24.085 --> 00:03:27.828
"How are we supposed to figure out if Wyssa or Morb is here?"

63
00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:29.873
Gliss mopped her brow.

64
00:03:29.893 --> 00:03:35.777
"It seems like the kind of place Morb would like—dangerous and scary."

65
00:03:37.398 --> 00:03:41.261
A scraping sound came from behind a house-sized boulder nearby.

66
00:03:41.281 --> 00:03:43.582
"Shh," Zann whispered.

67
00:03:43.602 --> 00:03:46.024
"That could be an unfriendly dragon."

68
00:03:46.965 --> 00:03:48.426
He tiptoed around the boulder.

69
00:03:49.186 --> 00:03:51.188
A teenage boy was scraping at the dirt.

70
00:03:51.208 --> 00:03:53.469
"Hey!" Zann blurted out.

71
00:03:53.489 --> 00:03:54.750
"It's a person!"

72
00:03:55.591 --> 00:03:56.631
The boy spun around.

73
00:03:56.651 --> 00:03:58.656
"Oh! You startled me!"

74
00:03:58.897 --> 00:03:59.517
he exclaimed.

75
00:03:59.537 --> 00:04:02.518
"Sorry. My name is Zann."

76
00:04:02.538 --> 00:04:05.959
"I'm Arrano," the boy replied with a smile.

77
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.741
By then Zann's friends had appeared, and Zann quickly introduced them.

78
00:04:10.761 --> 00:04:13.102
"What's the name of this world?"

79
00:04:13.402 --> 00:04:14.503
Perda asked Arrano.

80
00:04:15.323 --> 00:04:16.604
Arrano looked surprised.

81
00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:18.304
"Don't you know where you are?"

82
00:04:18.325 --> 00:04:22.286
"We just arrived through a wormhole," Gliss explained.

83
00:04:23.066 --> 00:04:26.568
"Really? You came here, to Drac, from another world?"

84
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.322
Arrano's friendly expression changed to a worried one.

85
00:04:30.342 --> 00:04:32.904
"We don't get many visitors here.

86
00:04:33.285 --> 00:04:36.307
It would probably be best for you to leave before they see you."

87
00:04:36.327 --> 00:04:38.448
"Before who sees us?"

88
00:04:38.709 --> 00:04:39.349
Perda asked.

89
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.371
Arrano didn't answer.

90
00:04:41.831 --> 00:04:43.652
He was staring past the visitors.

91
00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:45.254
Zann turned.

92
00:04:45.774 --> 00:04:48.056
A pair of dragons had just waddled into sight.

93
00:04:48.856 --> 00:04:53.560
They were a little smaller than Zing but much plumper, with shiny blue scales.

94
00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:58.050
"Shoo!" Gliss said, waving her hands at the little dragons.

95
00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.531
"Get out of here!"

96
00:05:00.371 --> 00:05:01.412
The dragons ignored her.

97
00:05:01.832 --> 00:05:03.453
Darb watched them with interest.

98
00:05:03.473 --> 00:05:06.734
"They look a little like river hoppers, don't they?"

99
00:05:06.975 --> 00:05:07.475
he remarked.

100
00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:09.036
Zann nodded.

101
00:05:09.056 --> 00:05:12.077
"One of Boz's friends has a hopper as a pet.

102
00:05:12.497 --> 00:05:13.818
It's bigger than these though."

103
00:05:14.779 --> 00:05:16.720
He frowned as the dragons came closer.

104
00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.161
"And much less bold."

105
00:05:20.542 --> 00:05:24.364
He turned, planning to ask Arrano how to get rid of the pests.

106
00:05:25.248 --> 00:05:28.209
To Zann's surprise, Arrano was nowhere in sight.

107
00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:30.390
"Hey, where'd he go?"

108
00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.190
Darb wondered.

109
00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:32.690
Perda shrugged.

110
00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:35.411
"He seemed kind of nervous or something."

111
00:05:36.331 --> 00:05:39.752
"No wonder, living in a crazy world like this."

112
00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:40.793
Gliss shuddered.

113
00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.913
Zing was glaring at the approaching dragons.

114
00:05:44.674 --> 00:05:46.554
He sent out a warning blast of flame.

115
00:05:47.374 --> 00:05:48.815
The smaller dragons jumped back.

116
00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.276
Then one of them let out a sharp cry.

117
00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.661
The second one opened its mouth and shot out a stream of lava.

118
00:05:57.381 --> 00:05:59.082
"Whoa!" Zann jumped aside.

119
00:05:59.902 --> 00:06:03.343
The lava hit a shrub, which was instantly burned to a stump.

120
00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:07.884
"Okay, maybe they're not much like river hoppers after all," Darb said.

121
00:06:07.904 --> 00:06:09.585
"Let's get out of here!"

122
00:06:09.605 --> 00:06:11.165
"Good idea."

123
00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:12.786
Zann whistled for Zing.

124
00:06:12.806 --> 00:06:13.926
"Come on, boy!"

125
00:06:14.786 --> 00:06:19.588
Before Zing could get to Zann, one of the other dragons leaped up and batted him out of

126
00:06:19.628 --> 00:06:19.928
the air.

127
00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.582
Zing landed on the hard ground with a grunt and lay there stunned.

128
00:06:24.602 --> 00:06:26.903
"Zing!" Zann cried.

129
00:06:27.723 --> 00:06:31.945
He tried to rush over, but one of the blue dragons blocked him with another lava blast.

130
00:06:32.965 --> 00:06:33.566
"I've got him!"

131
00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:36.407
Darb dodged around the second dragon and grabbed Zing.

132
00:06:36.427 --> 00:06:38.508
"Darb! Look out!"

133
00:06:38.768 --> 00:06:39.468
Gliss screamed.

134
00:06:40.248 --> 00:06:45.751
Both dragons had turned toward Darb and Zing, who were now backed up against the huge boulder.

135
00:06:46.631 --> 00:06:48.192
The dragons moved closer.

136
00:06:49.691 --> 00:06:50.756
"Uh-oh!" cried Darb.

137
00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:53.850
"I can't get past them—we're trapped!"
